{
  "$comment": [
    "The curated global lookups (JJ-022): the vocabulary JiggerJot owns, not content lifted from any",
    "source book. Households cannot add to these in MVP, so this file is the whole of them.",
    "",
    "Ordering is display order and is deliberate: the common choice first, the exotic last, because a",
    "browse filter reads top-down. Names are what a person sees, so they are written the way a bartender",
    "would say them.",
    "",
    "Ids are not stored here. CatalogSeeder derives a stable GUID from the row's kind and name, so the",
    "same row keeps the same id on every environment and across every re-run — which is what lets a",
    "later seed pass reference these rows without a lookup table of its own.",
    "",
    "Adding a row is safe and additive. RENAMING one changes its derived id, which orphans every",
    "reference to it: treat a rename as a new row plus a migration for the old one."
  ],

