  "$unitNotes": [
    "A unit is convertible exactly when it carries a millilitreFactor; a Neutral unit leaves it null and",
    "always displays as authored (JJ-007, JJ-008). 'barspoon' is Neutral rather than a synonym for tsp on",
    "purpose: bar spoons run 2.5-5 ml depending on the spoon, so rendering '1 barspoon' as '5 ml' would",
    "invent a precision the recipe never had.",
    "",
    "'part' is what makes the proportional recipes of the older books expressible at all - a 1930 recipe",
    "reading '2/3 gin, 1/3 vermouth' has no absolute volume anywhere in it, and forcing one would be a",
    "fabrication. Stored as authored, displayed as authored.",
    "",
    "There is no unit for a whole item. '1 egg' is an amount with no unit, which the model already allows."
  ],

