  "$categoryNotes": [
    "Exactly two levels (JJ-015): a top-level category and its subcategories, no deeper. Filtering a",
    "parent matches every child, so 'all rum' is one query (JJ-016).",
    "",
    "The top level is the ingredient FAMILY, not a shelf section - 'Rum', not 'Spirits'. A three-level",
    "tree would be the natural next thought and is deliberately not modelled: it makes the parent-matches-",
    "children query recursive for a gain nobody asked for.",
    "",
    "There is no category for water or ice. They are assumed always available and are never modelled as",
    "blocking inventory (JJ-020), so an ingredient row for either would be a bug waiting to happen."
  ]
}
